{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8afa843992ea5b40cbddbef4dd2871f7259bd2ceb30ca3723cc632ab79da1e7e","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate / project portability criterion","key_entities":[".rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-portability.md",".rebar/criteria_routing.json","tests/unit/test_project_portability_criterion.py","tests/unit/test_project_portability_docs.py","docs/plan-review-gate.md","AGENTS.md","project.portability","Platform and venue","rebar explain"],"problem_keywords":["portability","CI provider","dependency","plan-review criterion","fallback","no-CI environment"],"propositions":["The portability criterion's Platform and venue matrix cell treats CI as one undifferentiated venue, leaving projects with no CI provider unnamed and undetectable as a portability gap.","A plan whose only trigger for recurring work is a specific CI system (e.g., GitHub Actions) with no operation-linked or in-process fallback breaks portability for adopters without that CI provider or without any CI.","The criterion detection text must split the CI cell to explicitly name both 'CI under any provider' and 'projects with NO CI provider at all', and add a rule stating that CI-specific-only triggers require a fallback or fire a finding.","Five files must be updated to effect the rule: the authoritative rubric prompt, its doc mirror, test pinnings for both, and a pointer in AGENTS.md."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787487864317624001,"uuid":"e00a6a1c-692e-45fa-94e2-06efc1cd3cab"}